   "source_id": "commons:66622462",
   "provider": "Wikimedia Commons",
   "title": "The Shanghai Huangpu River flows on (36273761652).jpg",
   "description": "The Shanghai Huangpu River flows on as our cruise progresses. To the left is the Bund area in the Puxi district and to the right is the upcoming Pudong district. Pudong is really huge though- Shanghai's Pudong International airport took me nearly two and a half hours to reach by car! Back to the scene on hand, the Huangpu River is known as the Mother River of Shanghai. It is 113-km in length and flows into the Yangtze River as it's last tributary. The Yangtze itself ends i nthe East China Sea. The Huangpu river cuts across Shanghai city, dividing it nearly into two region: Puxi (West Bank) and Pudong (East Bank). The western side or Puxi is home to “An Exhibition of International Buildings” with various international architectural styles and most of historical tourist attractions. The eastern side or Pudong is a recent development of the last few decades and is the new business and financial district boasting many awesome glass and steel towers, like Shanghai Oriental TV Pearl, Shanghai Tower, Shanghai World Financial Tower and Jinmao Tower. (Shanghai, China, May 2017)",
   "creator": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
